<http://data.silknow.org/object/3111d421-ec84-34c0-bd76-5a402ea1f561>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Korean women carried ornamental knife sets as a reference to chastity, one of the eight virtues defined by the Chinese philosopher Confucius. The other virtues were loyalty, filial piety, trust, righteousness, integrity, humility and brotherly love. Heroic women in Korean history and legend defended their chastity to the death."@en , "Ornamental knife and chopstick set; Korea, 1820-80, Late Choson dynasty"@en , "Ornamental dagger, unjangdo, with chased iron blade, silver mounts and chopsticks, blue silk hanging straps, silver button and loop. The set consists of knife, two chopsticks, sheath and silk hanging strap\n\nColour: Multicoloured"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/a93de1f8-e246-37c0-9dea-0a9a4ae944f4> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Ornamental dagger, unjangdo, with chased iron blade, silver mounts and chopsticks, blue silk hanging straps, silver button and loop. The set consists of knife, two chopsticks, sheath and silk hanging strap\n\nColour: Multicoloured"@en , "Korean women carried ornamental knife sets as a reference to chastity, one of the eight virtues defined by the Chinese philosopher Confucius. The other virtues were loyalty, filial piety, trust, righteousness, integrity, humility and brotherly love. Heroic women in Korean history and legend defended their chastity to the death."@en , "Ornamental knife and chopstick set; Korea, 1820-80, Late Choson dynasty"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/3111d421-ec84-34c0-bd76-5a402ea1f561/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "M.17-1928" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O34908> .

